================== CREATING S3_Bucket and Automate by Terraform:

. Prerequisite: 

        Terraform =========== connect by aws cli ============== s3 bucket

    1. So you have to Configure and install AWS CLi to ec2 instance.(aws cli v2 install)
      . Run the followning command
            curl "https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64.zip" -o "awscliv2.zip"
            unzip awscliv2.zip
            sudo ./aws/install
                  ||
            aws --version

    2. configure aws ami user in aws cli and  provide required permission.
      . Go to iam role and create user and give attach access policy.
      . Go to iam security Cred and create access key.
      . Go to ubuntu console and run command 'aws configure'
      . configure accesskey and secrete access key.
      . Ready to use aws by CLI.
      . aws s3 ls 

   3. Now go to cli and go to terraform file and create s3.tf file
     . Go to Terraform Registry and search configuration for s3
     . sample file creation :

      # sample file creation
           provider aws {
                       region = "ap-south-1"
                        }
           resource aws_s3_bucket mybuckets
                       {
                       bucket = "mybucketterraaa"
                tags = {
                       Name = "my -bucket"
                       Environment = "dev"
                       }
                       }
